{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WHSdME7MABuhNCMfJvz9bM","type":"tool_result","content":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/task_context/reviewer.md:2. **Gold Table 的 N 不一致是陷阱**：GB 评估 N=491，TWV Probe 评估 N=322。TWV Probe 看似 best (0.854) 但 scope-matched 比较（bootstrap shared N=322）GB=0.877 > TWV=0.854。当前 Table 呈现暗示 TWV Probe > GB，实际可能相反\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/task_context/history/reviewer/loop_4.md:- MF-3 scope matching worker 完成 → 验证 structural GB 在 6,122 probe test split 上的 F1，评估 36.9pp claim 是否需要修正\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/task_context/history/reviewer/loop_4.md:  1. 21.6pp claim（0.967 cross-agent GB vs 0.751 in-domain LLM）是**跨 scope 比较**——reviewers 已标记为 overclaiming，MF-3 的 matched-scope 计算可能显著改变这个数字\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/.venv/lib/python3.14/site-packages/torch/_dynamo/symbolic_convert.py:            # If the global scope matches that of the root frame, use handler in\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/.venv/lib/python3.14/site-packages/torch/_dynamo/symbolic_convert.py:            # If the global scope matches that of the root frame, use handler in\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/report.md:- e2-gb-matched-scope: GB on OH matched-scope test split (N=6,122 conf≥2) vs Probe zero-shot，回应 C2 \"36.9pp 范围不一致\"（准备中）\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T015115/worst/review_report.md:4. **Scope expansion or scope-matched claims (important).** Either add a third agent from a non-SE domain, or explicitly scope all claims to \"SE agent monitoring\" and adjust the title/abstract accordingly.\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/artifacts/review_reports/round_2.md:- **中期（commitment 前）**: 补充 matched-scope 评估（structural GB on 6K subset 或 probe on 150K）；补 LLM on OH 实验；分析 silver-gold gap。\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/artifacts/review_reports/round_1.md:Both numbers appear in abstract and introduction as core selling points, with caveats buried in footnotes and §6. Table 2's footnotes (a, b) are too dense and cannot fix the fundamental problem of cross-scope comparison. The paper's defense (\"comparing the LLM's easier in-domain setting against structural's harder cross-agent regime\") is undermined by the fact that cross-agent structural evaluation uses silver labels from the same LFs. Fix: report all methods on the same evaluation scope; use matched-scope numbers in abstract/intro.\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/artifacts/review_reports/round_1.md:3. Report structural GB on same 6,122 test split as probe; use matched-scope numbers in abstract\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/ROADMAP.md:| D068 | 2026-05-15 | Headline gap 定为 19.6pp（in-domain scope-matched: 0. | llm-judge-strengthened, structural-core |\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/ROADMAP.md:| D067 | 2026-05-15 | Headline gap 采用 19.6pp scope-matched (in-domain 0. | llm-judge-strengthened, structural-core, structural-cross-agent |\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/paper_framing.md:- **Our framing (D072 Upgrade)**: 从 stagnation detection 到 compute-efficient intervention 的完整框架。**四层贡献**：(1) **Zero-Shot Transfer Dominance (primary)** — 结构特征在零样本跨 agent 迁移上大幅领先 probe（+39.4pp matched-scope）和 best LLM judge（+16.8pp），且仅需 2-LF deployable config（无 privileged outcome 信息）即可在 conf≥2 上达到 0.978 F1——结构特征是零数据部署的默认选择；(2) **Detection-to-Intervention (D072 新增)** — 将检测器输出转化为 early termination policy，回溯量化 compute waste 并模拟不同 threshold 下的 precision-recall-savings trade-off——建立从 detection research 到 deployment value 的直接桥梁；(3) **LF Temporal Dynamics Analysis** — 量化 LFs 在 agent trajectory 上的时序角色 + label quality as transfer bottleneck + circular evaluation 方法论贡献；(4) **TLM Negative Finding** — 三种 temporal label model 均未超越 MV，提供 failure analysis 约束未来研究。\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/paper_framing.md:- **Headline result template**: \"We present a framework for real-time LLM agent stagnation monitoring that bridges detection and compute-efficient intervention. Our central finding is that lightweight structural features (<5ms per window) dominate zero-shot cross-agent transfer: 30 features achieve 0.995 in-domain and 0.967 cross-agent F1 with no target domain data, outperforming a zero-shot neural probe by 39.4pp (matched-scope) and the best LLM judge by 16.8pp. A deployable 2-LF configuration (without privileged task outcomes) maintains 0.978 F1 on high-confidence labels. We translate detection into actionable intervention: retrospective compute waste analysis reveals X% of agent execution occurs after stagnation onset, and early termination simulation shows structural detectors can save Y% compute while preserving Z% task success — establishing a Pareto-optimal operating frontier. Our analysis uncovers that labeling functions exhibit agent-specific temporal dynamics and that label quality, not model architecture, is the dominant cross-agent transfer bottleneck. Three temporal label model implementations all fail to improve over simple majority vote, providing a well-characterized negative result. Human-annotated gold validation (505 windows, 3 annotators) confirms structural advantage over silver labels (GB 0.839 vs MV 0.798, p<0.001).\"\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/paper_framing.md:| Architecture novelty 不足 | 论文升级为 framework paper——novelty 在于从 detection 到 intervention 的完整链路 + matched-scope evaluation 方法论 + 2-LF deployable 配置设计，不在架构 |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01VxqiVJ87aTR1C8rGYzvz9z","session_id":"b07a11b6-c8ab-4699-acee-a0e26907aaa6","uuid":"dbc2fe5d-e123-4ec1-9d47-f87521b004af","timestamp":"2026-05-15T14:38:39.585Z"}
